\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"76c75ffa-1112-452d-9cec-46f0571e8317"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Why it's built this way: Abstract atoms until the end",
  FontWeight->Bold],
 "\n\n",
 "The explicit entries contain couplings and shape functions; G built from \
them would contain them many times over, and every later expression (loop \
integrands, their projections, the frequency integrals) would grow \
accordingly. With one atom per entry coefficient, G stays a small rational \
function of a handful of symbols, the heavy algebra of lessons 07",
 StyleBox["\[Dash]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "10 runs on it, and the atoms are replaced by their values only once, at \
assembly (lesson 11). This is rule 1 of the computer-algebra rules in the \
shallow-water project primer, \"abstract until the end\" (",
 StyleBox["~/sync_cnrs/Projects/shallow_water/AGENT_PRIMER.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " ",
 StyleBox["\[Section]",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "7, cited in ",
 StyleBox["design/FRGDESIGN.md",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 ", module 5). The atoms are curried, ",
 StyleBox["GammaAtom[a, b, m][s]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " (",
 StyleBox["Curried definitions",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 StyleBox[" (Glossary, lesson 02)",
  FontSlant->Italic,
  FontColor->GrayLevel[0.4]],
 "), because the same coefficient is needed at different momenta, q",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 " and (q + p)",
 StyleBox["\.b2",
  FontFamily->"Noto Sans"],
 "; ",
 StyleBox["ExactlyZeroQ",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " treats each ",
 StyleBox["GammaAtom[...][s]",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
  Background->GrayLevel[0.92]],
 " as one atom with its own random value (lesson 00, section 5)."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{4, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->GrayLevel[0.55],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.93, 0.93, 0.93],ExpressionUUID->"6780f31c-73ad-42b1-b72d-076ecde86b99"],

Cell["2. From \[CapitalGamma]2 + R to atoms", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"e96f9893-1206-49a8-a8e1-fb2ae2e2aeae"],

Cell["\<\
(* Kernel/Propagator.wl:28-52 *)
BuildPropagator[vertices_, regulator_] := Block[{$FRGModule = \
\"Propagator\"},
  Module[{t0 = AbsoluteTime[], fields, theory, phis, bars, n, nf, pos, g2, \
rm, full, atoms = {}, atomVals = <||>, abs, iphi, ibar, B, Bm, C,
    detB, deg, cs, G, checks = {}, warns = {}, stage, valid, explanation, \
ex},
   validateStage[vertices, \"Vertices\"]; validateStage[regulator, \
\"Regulator\"];
   FRGAssert[\"Propagator.sameAnsatz\", regulator[\"Upstream\"] === vertices[\
\"Upstream\"], {regulator[\"Upstream\"], vertices[\"Upstream\"]},
    \"the regulator and the vertices were built from different ansatz \
stages\"];
   theory = vertices[\"Ansatz\"][\"Theory\"]; fields = vertices[\"Fields\"]; \
phis = theory[\"Scalars\"]; bars = theory[\"ResponseFields\"];
   nf = Length[fields]; n = Length[phis]; pos[a_] := \
First[FirstPosition[fields, a]];

   (* explicit Gamma2 + R, polynomial in w *)
   g2 = Gamma2Matrix[vertices, ww, qv] /. scal[qv, qv] -> ss;
   rm = RegulatorMatrix[regulator, ss];
   full = Expand[g2 + rm];
   FRGAssert[\"Propagator.polynomial\", AllTrue[Flatten[full], PolynomialQ[#, \
ww] &], full, \"Gamma2 + R must be polynomial in w\"];

   (* abstract atoms: coefficient of (I w)^m of entry (a, b), a <= b; numbers \
stay numbers *)
   abs = Table[Module[{i0 = Min[i, j], j0 = Max[i, j], e, a, b},
      a = fields[[i0]]; b = fields[[j0]]; e = full[[i0, j0]];
      Sum[Module[{c = Expand[Coefficient[e, ww, m] / I^m]},
        Which[c === 0, 0, NumericQ[c], c,
         True, (If[! KeyExistsQ[atomVals, GammaAtom[a, b, m]], \
atomVals[GammaAtom[a, b, m]] = Function[Evaluate[{ss}], Evaluate[c]]];
          GammaAtom[a, b, m][ss])] (I If[i <= j, 1, -1] ww)^m], {m, 0, \
Exponent[e, ww]}]], {i, nf}, {j, nf}];
   atoms = Keys[atomVals];
   AppendTo[checks, assertCheck[\"Propagator.atomsReal\", FreeQ[(#[ss] & /@ \
Values[atomVals]), Complex], atomVals,
     \"the coefficients of (I w)^m must be real (no explicit I in the ansatz \
or the regulator)\", ToString[Length[atoms]] <> \" real entry atoms\"]];\
\>", "Program",ExpressionUUID->"694862ce-19f0-4ee8-960b-a6bef3fce354"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Propagator.sameAnsatz",
  FontFamily->"Source Code Pro",
  FontColor->RGBColor[0.6, 0.12, 0.1],
